From 1d549381031672290cb10fd07e961b862cdc090b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinn <coderquinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:44:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(access): complete session-ending stop once a published
 core is reaped

StopAllForSessionEnding no longer waits for its 10 s timeout when an internal core has published Ready. The session-ending path completes after forwarding stops and the owned child is reaped, while the held listener and network_lease_pending_ stay in place until the Network fence or process exit. Adds a test-only canary bypass (CHECK_IS_TEST) to reach Ready in the integration test.
---
 ...cess_internal_core_manager_mac_unittest.cc | 63 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../aegis/access/access_local_core_manager.cc | 42 +++++++++++--
 .../aegis/access/access_local_core_manager.h  |  7 ++-
 3 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/aegis/access/access_internal_core_manager_mac_unittest.cc b/chrome/browser/aegis/access/access_internal_core_manager_mac_unittest.cc
index a21a67c1ca55fe3f6a0202aed833e12fc0c9862a..8b1efedb3f38a3bda0b7d9ea2cb13379b80c07ab 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/aegis/access/access_internal_core_manager_mac_unittest.cc
